        <title type="html"><![CDATA[Link Chromium bug for unsupported `:lang()` selector ranges in Chrome]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29642</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29642"/>
        <updated>2026-05-10T06:27:01.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12870451?u=53865490ebd18b730e5c7a1383496f38d641ab27&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/>
<h4 dir="auto">Summary</h4>

<p dir="auto">Chromium browsers do not implement the Selectors 4 <code class="notranslate">:lang()</code> forms that use comma-separated ranges (<code class="notranslate">:lang(A, B)</code>) or wildcard subtags (<code class="notranslate">:lang(*-C)</code>), despite supporting the base pseudo-class. This updates the BCD entries so those unsupported subfeatures point to the tracked Chromium bug.</p>
<ul dir="auto">
<li>Copilot's PR: <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="4414418964" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/tats-u/browser-compat-data/issues/3" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/tats-u/browser-compat-data/pull/3/hovercard" href="https://github.com/tats-u/browser-compat-data/pull/3">tats-u#3</a></li>
<li>Copilot's log: <a href="https://github.com/tats-u/browser-compat-data/sessions/bf851ef8-8cf2-4756-9301-31bb657bb47f">https://github.com/tats-u/browser-compat-data/sessions/bf851ef8-8cf2-4756-9301-31bb657bb47f</a></li>
</ul>
<h4 dir="auto">Test results and supporting details</h4>


<ul dir="auto">
<li>
<p dir="auto"><a href="https://crbug.com/40811938" rel="nofollow">https://crbug.com/40811938</a> (<a href="https://issues.chromium.org/issues/40811938" rel="nofollow">https://issues.chromium.org/issues/40811938</a>)</p>
<blockquote>
<p dir="auto">Steps to reproduce the problem:<br>
1.Use asterisk or comma in language range for :lang() pseudo element selector.<br>
2. Or open langSelectors.html file in Chrome on Windows.</p>
<p dir="auto">What is the expected behavior?<br>
Should work as per the W3 specifications: <a href="https://drafts.csswg.org/selectors/#the-lang-pseudo" rel="nofollow">https://drafts.csswg.org/selectors/#the-lang-pseudo</a></p>
<p dir="auto">What went wrong?<br>
None of the language range selectors, which are valid by W3 specs, work.<br>
They work on iPadOS Chrome and Safari browsers though.</p>
</blockquote>
</li>
</ul>
<h4 dir="auto">Related issues</h4>


<p dir="auto">None</p>]]></content>
